**Read:** [Meep — methods, tutorials, validation and licence](../sources/Meep-Methods-Manual.lingua#r_7V0TJSMDBGNHBD0MBTB94W8GRX), convergence and discretization guidance; [Understanding the Finite-Difference Time-Domain Method — John B. Schneider](../sources/Understanding-FDTD-Schneider.lingua#r_3BTKKSTADJQXT1XD3S4WZVBMYM), numerical dispersion and verification development.

Convergence concerns a specified quantity as an approximation is refined. Compare potential, peak field, total charge, force and energy separately; a singular ideal edge can make peak field diverge while integrated quantities converge. Report the geometry and regularization rather than hiding the singularity with plotting limits.

For the one-dimensional Poisson example with ε = 1 and sinusoidal source, derive the discrete eigenvalue λ_h = 4sin²(πh/2)/h². The discrete nodal amplitude is π²/λ_h times the sine mode. This gives an exact discrete benchmark and predicts second-order continuous error for small h. Use three or more refinements and check that the measured regime is asymptotic before estimating order.

Vary mesh, computational domain, source representation and algebraic tolerance independently. An error budget should identify which approximation each change probes. A manufactured solution validates an implementation for the chosen mathematical problem, not the constitutive law for a specimen. State numerical accuracy relative to the decision or physical uncertainty: many digits in an output file do not establish equally accurate material or geometric input. Reuse the computational-validation Record for independent oracles and reproducible reporting.

